<title>UK: Tarmac could see rise in goodwill for PSA.</title>
<headline>Tarmac could see rise in goodwill for PSA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction group Tarmac Plc said on Friday that a review into the terms to buy PSA Projects from the British government's Department of the Environment had resulted in a decision which could increase the level of goodwill for the buy by 14 million stg.</p>
<p>This payment, subject to Tarmac reviewing the judgement made by an independent expert appointed to assess elements of the deal, would come from Tarmac's shareholder funds in the 1996 accounts &quot;but will not affect the 1996 trading result&quot;, the company said.</p>
</text>
